# WhatsCLI — Cursor AI Rules
# Terminal-based WhatsApp client in Go 1.24 (whatsmeow + tview)

# Build & Test
# make build    → go build -o whatscli
# make test     → go test -race ./...
# make vet      → go vet ./...
# Requires CGO (SQLite). Linux: apt install gcc

# Architecture: two packages
# - main (root): TUI layer using tview (ui_layout.go, ui_handler.go, ui_keybindings.go, ui_render.go, ui_helpers.go)
# - messages/: business logic, WhatsApp connection, SQLite storage, command dispatch
# - config/: INI configuration with XDG paths
# - qrcode/: ANSI QR code rendering
# Communication: UI → CommandChannel → SessionManager.runManager() event loop
# Backend → UiMessageHandler interface (17 methods) → UI updates

# Command Pattern
# All commands registered in cmd_registry.go via init()
# Handler signature: func(sm *SessionManager, client *whatsmeow.Client, cmdName string, params []string)
# To add: create handler in cmd_*.go, register in init(), update PrintHelp() in ui_helpers.go

# Concurrency (CRITICAL)
# - ALWAYS use sm.getClient() — never read sm.client directly (data race)
# - Hold sm.mu ONLY for PQ/map mutations — release BEFORE SQLite writes (deadlock risk)
# - Use snapshotPQ() for safe priority queue reads from UI goroutine
# - All channels are buffered (size 10)
# - sm.reconnecting flag prevents duplicate reconnect goroutines

# Storage
# SQLite with WAL mode, 5s busy timeout
# Tables: conversations (JID PK), messages (ID PK, indexed on chat_id and chat_id+timestamp)
# No in-memory caches — all reads query SQLite directly
# Production: config.GetSessionFilePath() + "_meta.db"
# Testing: use InitWithDB() with in-memory SQLite (:memory:)

# Error Handling
# - Return errors, wrap with fmt.Errorf("context: %w", err)
# - Propagate to sm.uiHandler.PrintError(err)
# - NEVER use panic() for normal error handling
# - Use checkParam() for command parameter validation

# Code Style
# - One function per command
# - Document all exported functions and types
# - Use config.GetSessionFilePath() and XDG — never hardcode paths
# - Table-driven tests with -race flag
# - MockUiHandler from mock_ui_handler.go for backend tests
